# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the akari ASan test runs.
#
# These suppress leaks that originate in PHP/Zend internals or third-party
# libraries we link against, not in akari's own code. Keep this list tight:
# only add an entry when you've confirmed the allocation is not owned by us.
# A leak whose top akari-owned frame appears in the stack must NOT be
# suppressed here — fix it instead.

# PHP keeps interned strings and one-time module globals for the life of the
# process; LSan reports them at shutdown as "still reachable".
leak:zend_interned_strings_init
leak:zend_string_init_interned
leak:php_module_startup

# OpenSSL / libcurl one-time global init allocations.
leak:CRYPTO_zalloc
leak:curl_global_init
